{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "advection_1d_inflow_ppm",
    "description": "MMS driver: forced-steady 1-D linear advection u_t = -c D(u,x) + c dGdx on the unit interval [0, 1] with OPEN boundaries -- a prescribed inflow at the upstream (left) wall and a non-reflecting extrapolation outflow at the downstream (right) wall -- discretized by grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/ppm_D_inflow_bc (Piecewise Parabolic Method, Colella-Woodward 1984; conservative finite-volume semi-discrete method-of-lines flux, one-sided PPM reconstruction using the inflow ghost gL at the left wall and zeroth-order extrapolation at the right wall). This is the open-boundary PPM companion of problems/advection_1d_ppm_periodic.esm and the PPM analogue of problems/advection_1d_inflow_lax_friedrichs.esm / advection_1d_inflow_upwind.esm. SMOOTH-MONOTONE MMS (why cos(pi x), not the periodic sine): the manufactured STEADY solution u*(x) = cos(pi x) is MONOTONE on [0,1] with NO interior extrema, so the CW84 monotonicity limiter (which clips smooth extrema to first order -- the sub-nominal-order mechanism documented for the periodic PPM case) stays INACTIVE in the interior and the interior runs near its formal high order; the global observed order is therefore set by the ONE-SIDED boundary reconstruction, which is exactly what this open-boundary case is meant to measure. The exactly matching steady forcing is c dGdx with dGdx = g'(x) = -pi sin(pi x) (the analytic derivative of u*), so the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_x + c u*_x = 0 and u(t) = u* for all t; the discrete field drifts only by the operator truncation error (forced-steady MMS: observed order = operator order at t=0.1). INFLOW/OUTFLOW COMPATIBILITY (why cos(pi x) with c = 1, gL = 1): flow is in +x (c = 1 > 0), so the inflow is the left wall and the inflow value must equal the exact wall value gL = u*(0) = cos(0) = 1; the profile must have g'(0) = 0 at the inflow wall so the constant-gL upstream ghost matches the wall datum to O(dx^2) and the boundary-cell residual stays consistent with the interior (a nonzero wall gradient would pollute the order). The outflow (right) wall carries no external data -- the zeroth-order extrapolation ghost u[N+1]=u[N] is O(dx^2) accurate there because u*_x(1) = 0, and the reconstruction reaches only interior/self data (non-reflecting), so it needs no compatibility condition. cos(pi x) has u*_x = -pi sin(pi x) with u*_x(0) = 0 and u*_x(1) = 0, so both walls are clean and the global error is dominated by the one-sided reconstruction order (pinned honestly in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_inflow_ppm/golden/errors.json). CONSERVATION: the interior PPM flux-difference telescopes (neighbouring cells share the identical float face flux), but the domain is OPEN (mass enters through F_{1/2}=gL and leaves through the outflow), so unlike the periodic PPM case sum(u) is NOT globally invariant and there is NO mean-conservation assertion here. GRID CONTRACT WIRING (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0, 1]: x0 = 0 (parameter) and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing the extent by the metaparameter name N, esm-spec 9.7.6, so the convergence sweep's loader-API rebinding of N keeps dx consistent). gL is the rule's inflow free name, declared here as a parameter equal to the wall value; it lives only in the runtime rule body, never in a build-time ic/reference. The ic, the dGdx forcing, and the test references spell x_i = x0 + (i - 1/2) dx inline with load-foldable scalars (0 + (i - 1/2)(1/N)); the build-time 6.6.5/ic/observed cellwise evaluation is scope-free, so build-time coordinate expressions fold from literals and the metaparameter name N alone (never the free-name x_coord template).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:advection",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Colella, P., & Woodward, P. R. (1984). The Piecewise Parabolic Method (PPM) for gas-dynamical simulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 54(1), 174-201.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(84)90143-8"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2002). Finite Volume Methods for Hyperbolic Problems. Cambridge University Press. Chapter 6 (high-resolution / PPM reconstruction) and Section 7 (inflow / outflow boundary conditions for advection)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "AdvectionPPMInflow": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/ppm_D_inflow_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Advected tracer field over the x index set."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Constant transport speed (non-negative; the PPM upwind flux assumes flow in +x, inflow at the left wall). Multiplies both the discretized derivative and the manufactured forcing, so the steady MMS balance holds for any value."
        },
        "gL": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Inflow value carried into the domain at the left wall x = x0 (the rule's inflow free name). Set to the exact manufactured wall value u*(0) = cos(0) = 1 so the boundary cell is consistent; a generic no-inflow consumer would leave the rule's default of 0."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "dGdx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^4",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Analytic derivative of the manufactured solution: dGdx(x) = g'(x) = -pi sin(pi x). Constant in time; c dGdx is the manufactured forcing that holds u* = cos(pi x) steady. Cell centers x_i = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N are spelled inline from literals and the metaparameter name N (build-time-foldable; never the free-name x_coord template)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "cos",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  3.141592653589793,
                  {
                    "op": "faq",
                    "output_idx": [
                      "i"
                    ],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": {
                      "i": {
                        "from": "x"
                      }
                    },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        0,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      "c"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "D",
                    "args": [
                      "u"
                    ],
                    "wrt": "x"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "c",
                  "dGdx"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "N"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dGdx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                -3.141592653589793,
                {
                  "op": "sin",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        3.141592653589793,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_steady_inflow_ppm",
          "description": "Manufactured steady solution u*(x) = cos(pi x) with c = 1 and left inflow gL = u*(0) = 1. Derivation: the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_x + c u*_x = 0 with u*_x = dGdx = -pi sin(pi x), so u(t) = u* exactly; the discrete drift at t=0.1 is the pure truncation of ppm_D_inflow_bc. The profile is monotone (no interior extrema), so the CW84 limiter is inactive in the interior and the observed order is set by the one-sided boundary reconstruction; u*_x(0) = 0 and u*_x(1) = 0 keep both walls clean (metadata.description). References evaluate at cell centers x_i = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (reference equals the initial field). The t=0.1 assertion bounds the truncation-driven drift against the SAME steady reference (well under the 0.05 bound at the default N=64). Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_inflow_ppm/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.1
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      3.141592653589793,
                      {
                        "op": "faq",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.1,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.05
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      3.141592653589793,
                      {
                        "op": "faq",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
